    "body": "## Summary\n- add a central reviewed Stripe API version contract for the current `stripe-java` schema (`2026-07-29.dahlia`)\n- fail application startup before configuring the Stripe API key if the SDK's pinned `Stripe.API_VERSION` drifts\n- reject signed financial webhook events whose immutable `event.api_version` differs from the reviewed schema before any settlement service runs\n- keep unrelated/unhandled webhook event types ignored with HTTP 200 to avoid retry storms\n- add startup, contract and signed-webhook regression tests\n- document the controlled Stripe SDK/API upgrade procedure and explicitly forbid unsafe version overrides / unsafe webhook deserialization\n\n## Why\n`stripe-java` pins generated models and outgoing requests to a concrete Stripe API version. A dependency upgrade can therefore change payment semantics even if Java code still compiles. This makes that change fail closed and forces an explicit reviewed migration.\n\n## Financial safety\n- no wallet/ledger/settlement semantics changed\n- no provider calls added\n- no Stripe-Version override used\n- no `deserializeUnsafe()` used\n- mismatched financial webhook schemas are rejected before payment/refund/dispute/payout services are invoked\n\n## Schema\nNo Flyway migration.\n\n## Merge gate\nMerge only after exact-head Maven/API tests, webhook/payment/payout financial smokes, CodeQL, container security and full runtime CI are green; verify `master` is unchanged and the branch is 0 commits behind.",
